25,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"It turns out we are billed by area, not headcount, so empty desks still cost us. Also, re-running power for each desk is quite expensive.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Minato,,"The noise is much louder by the printer, and the physio says it takes days of small adjustments to get a workstation feeling right.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,May,,"Setting up a desk every morning takes up to nine minutes, and past unplanned shuffles caused weeks of interruptions and boxes everywhere.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"The current plan leaves some people without windows, which was a major complaint. Also, arrival times vary wildly, from 8 AM to 10 AM.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"Sitting close together really helped with handovers last spring, and the new joiners said they learned the unwritten rules just by overhearing us.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@May, if shuffles are that disruptive, we should avoid any system that requires frequent moving.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Shunichi, if some seats are worse than others, we need a way to make that fair.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,May,,"@Victoria, I agree. And if the morning setup takes nearly ten minutes, a daily change would be a waste of time.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Minato, exactly. If we have a first-come system, the early birds always get the windows and the quiet spots.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Victoria, but if we stay too rigid, do we lose the benefit of the new joiners learning from us?","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Daisuke, we can group people without moving them every day. The cost of re-running power makes frequent changes unsustainable.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Minato,,"I'm worried that if we don't have fixed spots, I'll never get my chair and monitor adjusted properly.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,May,,"@Minato, that sounds like a nightmare. I can't imagine spending my morning fighting with a monitor arm.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"It seems we have a conflict between the need for stability and the need for fairness regarding the ""bad"" seats.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,I just want to make sure we don't end up isolated from each other.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"The budget is tight, and the area billing is already a burden. We can't afford expensive facility changes.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,4,talk,Minato,,I really think the physical comfort and noise levels need to be a priority in the final choice.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,4,talk,May,,"I'm leaning toward whatever minimizes the daily ""setup"" time and the chaos of moving boxes.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"If we want to avoid the ""window lottery,"" we need a system that doesn't rely on who arrives first.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I agree that proximity is key for the team's growth, especially for the newer members.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
