50,3,1,talk,Victoria,,Option A is the most stable and cheapest for the budget since it avoids re-running power and network repeatedly.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Minato,,"Option A lets me fix my chair and avoid the printer noise, but Option B would mean everyone shares the bad spots.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,May,,Option C is out for me. I can't spend ten minutes every morning plugging in screens and cables.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Option C is unfair because of the arrival times. Option B is fairer, but Option A is the most decisive.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"Option A keeps us in functional groups, which is great for communication, but Option B might help us bond more.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Minato, Option B would trigger those facility charges every time the block rotates. That's a waste of money.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@Victoria, I see. But if I'm stuck by the printer in Option A, it's a long time to suffer.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, the ""half-packed boxes"" from the shuffles May mentioned make Option B sound exhausting.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Minato, we could just assign the seats in Option A fairly, rather than letting it happen by habit.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"If Option A allows us to group by project, I'm happy with that. It supports the joiners.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Victoria,,I vote for Option A. It's the only one that respects the budget and the billing structure.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Minato,,"I'm torn, but if we can assign the quiet spots fairly, I'll go with A for the ergonomic stability.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,May,,I'm voting A. No morning setup and no fortnight of interruptions for me.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,I'll vote A. It's the most rational way to handle the window and noise issues through direct assignment.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I'll vote A as well. It keeps the project strands together and is stable.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
